(1) The Regional Government in efforts to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children conducts empowerment and awareness to families, parents and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling. (2) In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government makes efforts as follows: a. increasing the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;

b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services; c. opening employment opportunities for women;

d. building community participation and concern towards prevention of protection of women and children from acts of violence;

e. building and providing complete and easily accessible information systems; and

f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children victims of violence.

Article 10

(1) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 9, shall be implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:

a. social;
b. health;
c. education;
d. employment;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual; and
g. peace and order.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

Article 2

Implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence is carried out based on the principles of:

a. respect for human rights;
b. gender equality and justice;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of the victim; and
e. respect for the rights of women and children.

Article 20

(1) The Regional Government shall conduct guidance and supervision of the administration of protection for women and children victims of violence. (2) Guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:

a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. provision of facilities;
d. monitoring; and
e. evaluation.
(3) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) is aimed at realizing the objectives of protecting women and children victims of violence in accordance with minimum service standards.

Article 11

(1) The forms of services provided to women and children victims of violence, are as follows:

a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal aid;
d. repatriation;
e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal; and
f. psychological services.
(2) The forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the Regional Government and implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection; and d. mental and spiritual.In the implementation of services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may cooperate with Government agencies, other Regional Governments and the community. (3) Further provisions regarding the procedures for services for handling the protection of women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraphs (1), (2), and (3), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

