(2) P2TP2A managers who, in carrying out their duties of protection, services and recovery for victims of violence, violate the principles of administering protection, services and recovery may be subject to sanctions in accordance with P2TP2A internal mechanisms and sanctions in accordance with the provisions of applicable Laws and Regulations.

Article 11

(1) The forms of services provided to women and children victims of violence, are as follows:

a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal aid;
d. repatriation;
e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal; and
f. psychological services.
(2) The forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the Regional Government and implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection; and d. mental and spiritual.In the implementation of services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may cooperate with Government agencies, other Regional Governments and the community. (3) Further provisions regarding the procedures for services for handling the protection of women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraphs (1), (2), and (3), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

